"""The supplied 5-by-4 Studio grid owns positions; names and playable details follow it."""
REGIONS = {
 'Northeast district': ('Northwest District',(1,25),'Green western ridges descend toward the northwestern city wall. Greywatch Keep and the Emberfox pools overlook roads leading to Phoenix Wing and the upper residential streets. The maintained approaches are busy; wooded slopes beyond them grow quieter.'),
 'Evertree district': ('Evertree District',(1,30),'The Evertree rises above pale civic buildings, gardens and the northern residential quarter. Broad approaches connect the court, the Cloud District and the great avenue below. Public streets and controlled palace rooms have different access.'),
 'harbor district': ('Harbor District',(1,25),'Northern shore roads meet the working waterfront and Hydra Head Academy. Cargo sheds, homes, gardens and coastal farms share the approaches to Whitecrest Harbor. Beaconrest Lighthouse marks the offshore channel.'),
 'glowhaven islets': ('Whitecrest Isles',(1,25),'Rocky islands and sheltered channels lie beyond the harbor. Saltmere and Driftstone support ordinary island households, while the isolated skull-shaped Wraith Island receives controlled prison traffic. Weather and working boats shape everyday journeys.'),
 'sea or something': ('Bluecoil Reach',(8,35),'Open blue water surrounds distant reefs, the Gilded Albatross anchorage and an isolated serpent resting place. Sailors distinguish ordinary coastal passages from the waters around a sleeping great beast. Sudden swells and scarce landing places reward preparation.'),
 'southwest district': ('Southwest District',(1,25),'Western gates, Gryffin Tail and closely fitted residential streets occupy the southwestern city. Rougher Greyfield housing gathers outside the southern walls, beyond which the land rises into pines. Maintained streets remain ordinary civic ground.'),
 "worker's district": ('Artisan Quarter',(1,30),'Founders’ arcades, workshops, inns and the Crucible fill the central southern wards. Timber carts and students share the streets with shoppers and craftspeople. The lower wall separates working neighborhoods from the patched roofs of Greyfield.'),
 'southest district': ('Southeast District',(1,25),'Dragon Hoard, the eastern residential wards and the south gate overlook shore roads and neighboring farms. Commercial lanes connect the central city with Pebblewick and the coast. Workshops and quiet homes continue between the larger landmarks.'),
 'glowhaven shores': ('Crescent Coast',(1,25),'Curved beaches and small rocky islands follow the coast south of Whitecrest. Inns, fishers and visiting boats use the sheltered inshore water. Exposed reefs require care even when the nearby beaches are peaceful.'),
 'sea but with ruins': ('Moonarch Shoals',(10,35),'Broken island stonework, a stranded wreck and broad shell-shaped rocks interrupt the eastern sea. Fishers know usable approaches and signs of larger creatures passing beneath them. The wreck waters are considerably less forgiving than the sheltered island coves.'),
 'forests in west': ('Westpine Forest',(1,22),'Pines cover western ridges beside the lower river country. Clear working paths and old crossings skirt denser wildlife habitat. Woodcutters and walkers use the forest without treating every quiet clearing as a monster lair.'),
 'rivers': ('Pinewater Vale',(1,22),'Pinewater winds between wooded banks, farm tracks and the lanes around Pebbletown. Caravan staging and a remote alchemical cottage stand near the crossings. Water level, loose banks and ordinary animal activity give practical work to people who know the valley.'),
 'farmlands': ('Greenfield Farmlands',(1,22),'Cultivated strips and scattered homesteads spread beyond Greyfield and the city’s southern approaches. Irrigation branches lead toward the wider river country, while wooded margins conceal quieter ground. Farm roads carry produce, laborers and travelers.'),
 'cliffside near sea': ('Seaward Bluffs',(1,28),'Forested coastal bluffs give way to open meadows above a winding river. Starlark Abbey offers a settled presence inland, while the Seaward Overlook remains a quiet place to watch the sea. Exposed edges and weather demand sensible footing.'),
 'where the estuary is': ('Greenrush Marshes',(2,26),'The river breaks into shallow tidal channels, reed beds and sandbars before meeting the eastern sea. Boatwrights, fishers and field workers use its changing margins. Dry-looking ground can flood quickly with an incoming tide.'),
 'southwest forests': ('Southglade Woods',(3,25),'Southern woodland rises around an old stone lookout and scattered clearings. The outer tracks meet open grazing country; deeper folds of forest shelter wary animals. Old Southwatch can be reached without searching for a secret road.'),
 'another plains': ('Longgrass Meadows',(1,20),'Wide grasslands stretch between the western forest and the lower river. A few farmsteads and cart tracks leave large areas of open ground. Herding, gathering and ordinary rural travel occupy more of the landscape than ruins or fortifications.'),
 'plains': ('Sunmead Plain',(1,22),'Low hills, open pasture and scattered copses fill the southern plain. Thin dirt lanes link homesteads with the river crossings and neighboring meadows. Long sightlines let travelers notice weather, livestock and distant trouble before approaching.'),
 'west of village': ('Brookmeadow Downs',(1,22),'Open downs and the westward village approaches surround a working windmill. A crossroads links the northern road, river bridge and farm lanes. It is settled countryside with room for travelers to pass without becoming part of every local dispute.'),
 'brookmeadowVillage': ('Brookmeadow Vale',(1,20),'Brookmeadow’s houses, green and crop plots stand beside a river approach in the southeastern countryside. Farmers, mill customers and visiting workers share the lanes. The village remains a familiar local beginning within Glowhaven’s wider territory.')
}
ORPHANS={'Brookmeadow':'brookmeadowVillage','Glowhaven Farmlands':'farmlands','Shadowspire':'farmlands','Pinewater Woods':'forests in west','windmill':'west of village','an old guardtower':'southwest forests'}

# original placeholder -> (authored name, level band, public text, areas)
PLACES={
 'big ship location':('The Gilded Albatross',(15,36),'An ornate but hard-used sailing ship rides at a charted anchorage. Its butterfly-winged captain takes salvage work and agreed voyages, while crew members mend gear, cook and argue over their shares. Passage, employment and joining an expedition are separate arrangements.',[
 ('Boarding Landing','A boat comes alongside a rope ladder and guarded boarding rail. Visitors announce their business before climbing aboard.'),('Main Deck','Coiled ropes leave clear working lanes between the masts. Sailors repair canvas, secure loads and exchange news without stopping the ship’s work.'),('Quarterdeck','A broad rail overlooks the sails and sea. Reina Kazehara discusses routes and terms here when she is not needed elsewhere.'),('Galley','A swinging kettle hangs beside a compact stove and well-lashed stores. Nanae Kogure feeds the crew and guards her best seasoning.'),('Salvage Hold','Tagged crates, drying equipment and a small inspection table occupy the hold. Stored finds remain under their actual owner’s custody.'),('Crew Passage','Cabin doors and hammocks line a narrow, airy passage. Visiting passengers receive an agreed berth; other cabins remain private.')]),
 'shipwreck location, theres a kraken around here':('Splinterwake Wreck',(12,30),'A broken merchant hull lies among sharp eastern rocks. Low water exposes cargo spaces, but the approaches bear gouges far below the tide line. Large disturbances sometimes move through the surrounding water; an ordinary salvage trip need not challenge their source.',[
 ('Outer Anchorage','Sound water lies beyond the submerged spars. Boats can wait, observe the swell and choose whether to approach.'),('Broken Deck','Tilted planks and snapped ribs rise above the water. Lashings, safe footing and the changing tide matter more than speed.'),('Flooded Hold','Cold water covers loose cargo and low beams. Air, light and an actual way back are necessary for diving.'),('Deepwater Edge','The reef drops suddenly into dark water. Broad suckered marks on timber and unnatural swells warn of a great predator’s passing.')]),
 'island ruins location':('Moonarch Isle',(12,30),'A weathered stone arch and low foundations stand above a small rocky landing. Salt-resistant plants grow between old paving stones. Surveyors can study the remains without assuming the arch is an active portal.',[
 ('Pebble Landing','A sheltered shelf offers room to beach a small boat in fair conditions.'),('Broken Arch','One stone span still stands above cracked paving. Its surviving carvings reward patient copying rather than force.'),('Tide Crypt','A shallow undercroft opens from the lower foundations. Water stains mark when its passages become unsafe.')]),
 'rocky isle with a giant turtle':('Stillback Isle',(5,25),'A vast shell rests so quietly among the low rocks that it resembles part of the island. Mauruun grazes, sleeps and watches the water with immense patience. Fishers give the creature room and know better than to mistake stillness for helplessness.',[
 ('Quiet Landing','A small sheltered beach lies away from the creature’s head. Boats can land without stepping onto its resting ground.'),('Shell Garden','Weathered plates hold weed, harmless shell life and patches of old fishing line. The creature’s breathing shifts the ground beneath anyone who climbs aboard.'),('Nesting Shelf','Warm sand and low rocks form a protected resting shelf. Mauruun reacts strongly to harassment, injury or disturbance here.')]),
 'estuary':('Greenrush Estuary',(2,22),'Reed channels and pale sandbars divide the river’s meeting with the sea. Working skiffs follow changing water marks between the marsh and the coast. Fish traps, nesting birds and stranded debris offer ordinary work as well as reasons to explore.',[
 ('Skiff Landing','Daisaku Minobe’s timber supports hold small boats above the mud. Repairs and passage are arranged before a hull is taken.'),('Reedwalk','Raised footing follows a shallow channel where birds nest and fish flash beneath reeds.'),('Sandbar Crossing','The exposed bar offers a short route at low tide. Wet stakes and drift lines show how quickly its character changes.'),('Field Shelter','Sample jars, drying nets and a weather board crowd a modest covered workbench.')]),
 'alchemist hut in the boonies':('Thistlebank Alchemy Cottage',(1,25),'A low rural cottage smells of bruised herbs and warm copper. Yorina Tsugawa sells preparations by arrangement and complains loudly when customers mistake a difficult recipe for a miracle. A small garden and workroom support a real household as well as her experiments.',[
 ('Cottage Door','Plant trays and clean boots compete for space beneath a patched awning.'),('Copper Workroom','A sturdy bench carries labeled jars, a condenser and a basin for safely cooling mixtures.'),('Herb Plot','Raised beds grow ordinary useful plants alongside a few temperamental magical specimens.')]),
 'windmill':('Wrenhill Windmill',(1,20),'The windmill turns above scattered grain plots on Brookmeadow’s western approach. Customers wait with sacks while Shūhei Kusanagi counts loads and Fuyuka Kusanagi listens for mechanical trouble. Flour dust, local gossip and sibling arguments move through the yard together.',[
 ('Mill Yard','Wagons wait clear of the turning machinery and weighing platform.'),('Grinding Floor','Wooden gearing drives covered stones beneath a dust-worn beam. Work stops before anyone handles a jam.'),('Sail Gallery','An exposed gallery gives access to the sails and a wide view across the downs.')]),
 'an old guardtower':('Old Southwatch',(3,25),'An old lookout stands on a forested southern rise. Hirotaka Fushimi keeps its lower room habitable, mends what he can and considers unsolicited tracking advice an insult. Its view remains useful even though it no longer commands a garrison.',[
 ('Forest Steps','Roots cross the old stone approach; daylight makes the loose sections easy to notice.'),('Keeper’s Room','A stove, bedroll and carefully maintained tools occupy the lower room.'),('Lookout Walk','The upper walk overlooks the forest edge and open plain. Damaged masonry limits where it is safe to stand.')]),
 'rocky isle where a blue sea serpent is':('Bluecoil Rest',(20,35),'A great blue serpent sleeps across a remote reef, its body half hidden by clear water. Slow breathing lifts spray against the rocks, while shed scales catch beneath the tide line. Boats can observe from outside its reach; disturbing its resting ground risks waking a formidable animal.',[
 ('Distant Mooring','A bare outlying rock gives observers a place to secure a boat well away from the sleeping body.'),('Scale Shore','A narrow wash gathers naturally shed scales and drift. Fresh drag marks warn when the serpent has recently moved.'),('Serpent Ledge','The immense animal’s head and coils occupy the inner rocks. The ledge is its resting place rather than an ordinary landing.')]),
 'lighthouse':('Beaconrest Lighthouse',(1,24),'A red-capped offshore lighthouse guides boats through Whitecrest’s outer channels. Kōzō Hinoura keeps its light and stores in order with help from Saki Hinoura. Visiting crews bring supplies, repairs and more gossip than either keeper admits enjoying.',[
 ('Supply Jetty','A low jetty receives deliveries when the channel is usable.'),('Keeper’s Kitchen','Tea, charts and a drying rack share a warm little room beside the stores.'),('Lantern Room','Polished lenses surround a maintained light assembly. Its working parts are handled with the keepers’ permission.'),('Signal Balcony','Colored shutters and flags face the harbor approaches.')]),
 'a church or abbey?':('Starlark Abbey',(1,28),'White stone and a small bell tower rise above the southern river. The abbey is devoted to Avelune, Lady of Returning Light, and combines worship with a working hospice, gardens and guest rooms. Visitors need not share the faith to receive ordinary welcome or care.',[
 ('Pilgrim Court','Travelers wait beside a water basin and a shaded bench while attendants arrange beds or introductions.'),('Chapel of Returning Light','Lamps burn beneath a pale star-and-lantern image. Prayer and ceremony have their own rhythms beyond the day’s work.'),('Hospice','Clean linen, screens and herb-scented water surround a small number of beds. Patients are people with privacy, not an audience for every visitor.'),('Kitchen Garden','Useful herbs and vegetables grow along narrow paths watched over by Eiji Kuramochi.'),('Guest Wing','Plain rooms and a shared table shelter pilgrims, workers and people recovering from a difficult journey.')]),
 'gullwatch reefs':('Gullwatch Reefs',(3,22),'Low eastern reefs support nesting seabirds and pools bright with small marine life. Fishers know the usable channels and places to collect modest materials. Slippery stone and an incoming tide can turn an easy outing into a practical rescue.',[
 ('Boat Shelf','A shallow rocky shelf offers a temporary landing in fair water.'),('Tide Pools','Clear pools hold small creatures and useful shell fragments. Disturbing a nest can bring more trouble than the collection is worth.'),('Gull Ledges','High shelves overlook the channels and nesting grounds.')]),
 'crossroads':('Longgrass Crossroads',(1,20),'Three dirt roads meet between the northern approaches, river bridge and Brookmeadow’s western downs. A worn shelter gives travelers room to rest without blocking carts. News, lost animals and the occasional dishonest bargain pass through with the traffic.',[
 ('Way Shelter','A plain roof shelters a bench, water jar and a small space for travelers’ notices.'),('Cart Verge','Wagons can pull off the road here to change a wheel or compare routes.'),('Riverward Track','The southern branch follows open ground toward the bridge and village approach.')]),
 'cliff':('Seaward Overlook',(1,15),'A quiet grassy cliff looks out across the coast. Wind moves through the trees above a sheltered sitting place, while the exposed edge rewards care. Couples, walkers and solitary visitors can enjoy the view without finding a resident host.',[
 ('Sheltered Grass','A low bank blocks some of the wind and leaves room to sit together.'),('Sea Ledge','The open ledge gives a broad view of water and distant sails; its edge remains unguarded.')])
}

def apply(w):
    repairs=[]
    for place,parent in ORPHANS.items():
        old=w['locations'][place]['region'];w['locations'][place]['region']=parent
        repairs.append({'location':place,'oldRegion':old,'newRegion':REGIONS[parent][0]})
    regions={}
    for key,value in w['regions'].items():
        if key in REGIONS:
            name,band,text=REGIONS[key];value.update(name=name,basicInfo=text,npcLevelRange={'min':band[0],'max':band[1]},initialKnown=True);regions[name]=value
        else:regions[key]=value
    w['regions']=regions
    for value in w['locations'].values():
        if value.get('region') in REGIONS:value['region']=REGIONS[value['region']][0]
    rename={k:v[0] for k,v in PLACES.items()}
    locations={}
    for key,value in w['locations'].items():
        if key not in PLACES:locations[key]=value;continue
        name,band,text,parts=PLACES[key];keys=[name+' - '+label for label,_ in parts]
        areas={}
        for i,((label,description),area) in enumerate(zip(parts,keys)):
            paths=[keys[j] for j in range(len(keys)) if j!=i and (i==0 or j==0 or abs(i-j)==1)]
            areas[area]={'description':description,'paths':paths}
        value.update(name=name,basicInfo=text,hiddenInfo='',complexityType='complex',detailType='detailed',initialKnown=key not in ['rocky isle where a blue sea serpent is','shipwreck location, theres a kraken around here'],areas=areas,npcLevelRange={'min':band[0],'max':band[1]})
        locations[name]=value
    w['locations']=locations
    # The six fixed parent keys retain their exact supplied local x/y.
    assert all(v['region'] in w['regions'] for v in w['locations'].values())
    for name,text in {
      'Brookmeadow':'A small rural town in Glowhaven’s southeastern river country. Its green, mill lanes and working plots welcome locals, returning travelers and people finding a new place in village life.',
      'Pinewater River':'Pinewater winds through the wooded valley south of Glowhaven’s western wards. Bridges, working banks and shallow resting places link Pebbletown with the surrounding farms.',
      'Caravan Outpost':'A practical staging stop beside the southern Pinewater roads. Merchants rest loads, arrange onward hauling and compare road conditions before continuing toward the city or the countryside.',
      "Hermit's hut":'A small hut stands on a wooded ridge beyond the southwestern city approaches. Its remote-feeling setting and uneven path matter as much as the modest dwelling.',
      'Glowhaven Farmlands':'Grain, vegetables and irrigation strips spread beyond Greyfield and the southern city roads. Takumi Hatano organizes shared channel work, seasonal labor and produce arrangements among the growers.'
    }.items():
        # Preserve established supplemental opportunities while replacing the outdated opening paragraph.
        old=w['locations'][name]['basicInfo'].split('\n\n',1);w['locations'][name]['basicInfo']=text+('\n\n'+old[1] if len(old)>1 else '')
    return {'renamedRegions':{k:v[0] for k,v in REGIONS.items()},'renamedLocations':rename,'repairedOrphans':repairs}
